        "original_id": "2f036a49-171f-5477-9aad-1787545ff6a3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: NASA\n- People: Wernher von Braun\n- Projects: Applications Technology Satellites, ATS-2\n- Products: V-2 rocket, Saturn V\n- Places: Cape Canaveral\n\nFacts:\n- Wernher von Braun was born on March 23, 1912, and died on June 16, 1977.\n- Wernher von Braun was a German, later American, aerospace engineer and space architect.\n- Wernher von Braun is credited with inventing the V-2 rocket for Nazi Germany and the Saturn V for the United States.\n- NASA launched the Applications Technology Satellites as a series of experimental satellites under the supervision of, among others, Wernher von Braun.\n- NASA launched ATS-2, an Applications Technology Satellite communications satellite, on April 6, 1967.\n- ATS-2 launched on an Atlas-Agena D rocket from Cape Canaveral.",
